  </aside>
  <div class="content">
    <p class="review"><b>Medically reviewed by:</b> Dr. Kamran Saleem (MBBS 1988, UK Diploma in Genito-Urinary Medicine &amp; Venereology, University of Liverpool, 1998; PMDC Registered{pmdcNo ? ` (No. ${pmdcNo})` : ""}; 25+ years clinical reproductive experience) · <b>Last medically reviewed:</b> <time datetime={reviewed}>{reviewedLabel}</time> · Guidance informed by <a href="https://www.asrm.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASRM</a>, <a href="https://www.eshre.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ESHRE</a> and the <a href="https://www.who.int" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WHO</a> 6th Edition Laboratory Manual.</p>

    <section id="what">
      <p class="kick">Overview</p>
      <h2>What Is a Doctor-Led Fertility Assessment?</h2>
      <div class="snippet"><p>A doctor-led fertility assessment is a comprehensive medical evaluation of both partners to understand possible reasons for difficulty conceiving. It includes a review of reproductive and medical history, female ovulation and reproductive health, male reproductive health and semen analysis, followed by investigations selected according to individual clinical needs. Dr. Kamran Saleem provides fertility consultations in Lahore to help couples understand their findings and make informed decisions about their next steps.</p></div>
      <p>At Kamran Fertility Clinic, fertility assessment is not limited to ordering blood tests or checking sperm count. It involves understanding the couple's complete reproductive history, identifying possible contributing factors and deciding which investigations may be useful before recommending a treatment approach.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="compare">
      <p class="kick">Assessment or tests?</p>
      <h2>Understanding Fertility Assessment and Individual Diagnostic Testing</h2>
      <p>Understanding your fertility begins with distinguishing between a <b>Doctor-Led Fertility Assessment</b> (this page) and <b>Individual Laboratory Testing</b> (see <a href={TS}>fertility tests</a>).</p>
      <p>Many couples order standalone laboratory tests without first discussing their medical history with a fertility doctor. Although individual tests can provide useful information, their results need to be interpreted in the context of age, symptoms, reproductive history and the health of both partners. A fertility assessment brings this information together. It helps the doctor decide which tests are relevant, whether further evaluation is required and what the findings may mean for the couple.</p>
      <div class="tw"><table class="slim">
        <thead><tr><th>Feature / Scope</th><th>Doctor-Led Assessment</th><th><a href={TS}>Individual Diagnostic Tests</a></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{compare.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r[0]}</th><td>{r[1]}</td><td>{r[2]}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p>The main assessment page explains the complete clinical evaluation. The dedicated pages provide more detailed information about each partner: <a href={`${AS}/female-fertility-assessment`}>Female Fertility Assessment</a> and <a href={`${AS}/male-fertility-assessment`}>Male Fertility Assessment</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="when">
      <p class="kick">Timing</p>
      <h2>When Should You Book a Fertility Consultation?</h2>
      <p>Couples do not always know when it is appropriate to consult a fertility doctor. Some have been trying to conceive for several months, while others already have irregular menstrual cycles, abnormal semen analysis reports or a history of reproductive health problems. A fertility consultation helps identify which concerns need further evaluation and whether any investigations or referrals are appropriate.</p>
      <h3 class="sh">You may consider booking a fertility assessment if:</h3>
      <ul class="tick two">{when.map(w => <li>{w}</li>)}</ul>
      <p>Some people should seek an assessment earlier rather than waiting for the usual time periods. This can include people with known reproductive conditions, previous reproductive surgery, irregular or absent periods, or a history that may affect fertility. The 12-month and six-month timelines reflect the commonly used definition of infertility (see <a href="https://www.who.int" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WHO</a>, <a href="https://www.asrm.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASRM</a> and <a href="https://www.eshre.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ESHRE</a>). Female age is one of the most important factors, which is why waiting is not advised after 35.</p>
      <p class="actions2"><a class="btn sm" href={wa}>Ask about an appointment</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="partners">
      <p class="kick">Both partners</p>
      <h2>Male and Female Fertility Assessment: Why Both Partners Matter</h2>
      <p>Difficulty conceiving is not exclusively a female or male problem. Fertility depends on reproductive factors in both partners, and sometimes more than one factor contributes to a couple's difficulty becoming pregnant. For this reason, a complete fertility evaluation considers both partners rather than focusing on only one person's test results.</p>
      <p>At Kamran Fertility Clinic, the assessment considers the female partner's ovulation, ovarian reserve, hormones and reproductive anatomy alongside the male partner's sperm health, reproductive history and relevant hormonal factors.</p>
      <div class="cards c2">
        {mf.map(([h, i, p, bullets, more]) => (
          <div class="card svc"><span class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[i]} /></span><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p><ul class="tick">{bullets.map(b => <li>{b}</li>)}</ul><p class="more" set:html={more} /></div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h3 class="sh">Couple Fertility Consultation in Lahore</h3>
      <p>A couple fertility consultation brings both partners into the same evaluation process. Instead of investigating only the female partner or asking the male partner to undergo testing separately at a later stage, the doctor reviews the couple's reproductive history together. This approach helps identify whether the difficulty may involve female factors, male factors, a combination of both or an unexplained cause.</p>
      <p>During a couple fertility consultation, Dr. Kamran Saleem may review:</p>
      <ul class="tick two">{couple.map(c => <li>{c}</li>)}</ul>
      <p>Both partners are encouraged to attend together when possible. If one partner cannot attend, the initial consultation can still help establish the available history and identify what information may be needed.</p>
      <div class="snippet"><p><b>The objective is to understand the couple's fertility concerns as a whole, rather than treating male and female evaluation as unrelated processes.</b></p></div>
    </section>

    <section id="framework">
      <p class="kick">The process</p>
      <h2>The Five-Stage Fertility Assessment Framework</h2>
      <p>At Kamran Fertility Clinic, diagnostic evaluations follow a structured clinical approach designed to understand the couple's reproductive health, avoid unnecessary investigations and support informed decisions.</p>
      <ol class="tl">
        {stages.map((s, n) => (
          <li><span class="dot">{n + 1}</span><div>
